{"agent":"Monster3-fix-size-knobs-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The old implementation built the knob set from `dataclasses.fields(cls)`, so the function itself guaranteed that every `Knobs` field was populated from the corresponding `remote_*` config value (or failed loudly if that value was absent). The new explicit call no longer keeps that promise: if `Knobs` gains a field with a default, e.g. `max_lanes: int = 1`, and `Config.swarm` exposes `remote_max_lanes=5`, `from_config` returns `max_lanes=1` and silently ignores the configured knob. The comment says a test holds the field/knob lists together, but the production path can still be wrong whenever that test is not updated or not run; the change replaces a runtime invariant with a manual list.","digest":"0add938a1850fdd1","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py:from_config","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py:from_config"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new `prices.limit` and `prices.reset` entries make the dead-knob ratchet pass on a hard-coded allowlist without verifying the claimed reads. If `services/limit_routing.headroom` is changed so it no longer calls `PricesConfig.limit_of`/`reset_of` (or calls them only on a default `PricesConfig` rather than loaded config), `test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py` still passes because the names are exempted in this file, while the corresponding config knobs are actually dead. The comment’s “Pinned by tests/test_limit_routing.py” promise is not enforced by this test, so the ratchet can falsely report no dead knobs.","digest":"baee509b6a777879","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:62","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:62"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6063,"diff_sha":"19dba85682b3fea9b4a1922b9532d41d45bb11a6effd361b52debb74deb476af","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-size-knobs","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":4.3,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"7bd53699d63b3e2a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-size-knobs.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T133558Z-c3b2c3f9.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"8064d91a6411","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-fix-size-knobs-7267fe reviewed lane-drift-c's fix-size-knobs","reviewed_head":"11a7972aca62a4bd592fe71d90b2acf9985de383","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py":"100644 28ac4526f53e306eadaa482e6a82a4dbcbbbae5d","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.adapters.mcp.toml":"","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.adapters.mcp_wire.toml":"100644 05aa39e349492e936660bfdc67ca14e2a8a0d007","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.completion.scripts.toml":"100644 fde74118af8d10a39dc840ad20b4e5d4336a405c","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.completion.values.toml":"100644 3b71b16ac596919432e173ab7c4660f99677b932","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.metrics.runs_to_merge.toml":"100644 b67f6533138948f78678c646600fd878f5528046","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.output_budget.toml":"100644 84cc96d2854869b3147e5e1719d16e0fe05b2a1f","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.services.parity.reuse.toml":"100644 6b55eb5640ffa73448b8bc26c1d8e4b5c063cdbf","tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py":"100644 157061e5bf0cab286942253da7e50e6249956d36"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/swarm/remote_confi