{"agent":"Monster3-fix-size-knobs-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The old implementation built the knob set from `dataclasses.fields(cls)`, so the function itself guaranteed that every `Knobs` field was populated from the corresponding `remote_*` config value (or failed loudly if that value was absent). The new explicit call no longer keeps that promise: if `Knobs` gains a field with a default, e.g. `max_lanes: int = 1`, and `Config.swarm` exposes `remote_max_lanes=5`, `from_config` returns `max_lanes=1` and silently ignores the configured knob. The comment says a test holds the field/knob lists together, but the production path can still be wrong whenever that test is not updated or not run; the change replaces a runtime invariant with a manual list.","digest":"0add938a1850fdd1","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py:from_config","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py:from_config"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new `prices.limit` and `prices.reset` entries make the dead-knob ratchet pass on a hard-coded allowlist without verifying the claimed reads. If `services/limit_routing.headroom` is changed so it no longer calls `PricesConfig.limit_of`/`reset_of` (or calls them only on a default `PricesConfig` rather than loaded config), `test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py` still passes because the names are exempted in this file, while the corresponding config knobs are actually dead. The comment’s “Pinned by tests/test_limit_routing.py” promise is not enforced by this test, so the ratchet can falsely report no dead knobs.","digest":"baee509b6a777879","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:62","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:62"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new test claims to pin the `KNOWN_UNREAD` exemption by proving that `PricesConfig.limit_of` and `reset_of` read `self.limit` and `self.reset`, but it only assigns one value to each field and checks that the accessors return the corresponding hard-coded expected values. If `limit_of` is mutated to `return 5.0` and `reset_of` to `return \"1d\"` unconditionally, the test still passes even though neither accessor reads the config knobs anymore, and the dead-knob ratchet would still accept the `prices.limit` / `prices.reset` exemption. Thus the added test does not actually pin the claimed reads and the exemption can still outlive the read.","digest":"ebf9bd9aad0b7ab5","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:test_the_prices_accessors_read_the_knobs","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_ratchet_no_dead_knobs.py:test_the_prices_accessors_read_the_knobs"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"11a7972aca62a4bd592fe71d90b2acf9985de383","delta_raised":["ebf9bd9aad0b7ab5"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":2315,"diff_sha":"92448039cd76d4d9bca57e5da4da1dc98f2860f8e88852b0ca90e5c3cf0448ac","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 11a7972aca","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":7.5,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"649ae136090292ef","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-size-knobs.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T134517Z-7b08fdb8.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-fix-size-knobs-7267fe reviewed lane-drift-c's fix-size-knobs","reviewed_head":"85dd86193a585538536fbf2aceb85b4cbc078831","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/swarm/remote_config.py":"100644 28ac4526f53e306eadaa482e6a82a4dbcbbbae5d","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.adapters.mcp.toml":"","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.adapt